---
import Prose from './Prose.astro';
import { TECHCART_DOCS } from '../consts';
import { MILESTONES_SHIPPED, MILESTONES_TOTAL } from '../data/techcart';

const facts = [
  ['Shape', 'npm-workspaces monorepo, flat structure, three workspaces'],
  ['Shared core', 'One Express API, one MongoDB Atlas database'],
  ['Infrastructure', 'Managed platforms only — Vercel, Render, MongoDB Atlas'],
  ['Process', 'Feature-by-feature against a versioned SRS'],
  [
    'Status',
    `${MILESTONES_SHIPPED} of ${MILESTONES_TOTAL} milestones shipped; NFRs and launch readiness open`,
  ],
];
---

<Prose>
  <p>
    TechCart is a production-oriented, <strong>India-first</strong> e-commerce platform. A
    buyer-facing Next.js storefront and a React/Vite admin console sit on top of a single
    Node/Express API and a single MongoDB database — no business logic is duplicated between the two
    front ends.
  </p>
  <p>
    Everything runs on managed infrastructure: the two front ends deploy to Vercel, the backend to
    Render as a Docker service, and data lives in MongoDB Atlas. Payments go through Razorpay,
    images through Cloudflare R2, and background work through BullMQ. Redis was removed along the
    way — rate limiting and caching now use in-memory fallbacks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Work proceeds feature-by-feature against a version-tracked Software Requirements Specification:
    each feature updates the SRS, becomes a milestone, then an issue, then code. The catalog, auth
    (Google OAuth + OTP, admin 2FA, bearer-token sessions), cart, orders, Razorpay payments,
    dashboard and inventory are all shipped; the non-functional requirements and launch readiness
    are the remaining work.
  </p>
</Prose>

<dl class="mt-6 grid gap-x-6 gap-y-2 sm:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr]">
  {facts.map(([term, detail]) => (
    <div class="contents">
      <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-fg">{term}</dt>
      <dd class="text-sm text-muted">{detail}</dd>
    </div>
  ))}
</dl>

<p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted">
  Deeper detail lives in TechCart's own docs:
  <a
    href={TECHCART_DOCS.srs}
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    class="font-medium text-accent underline underline-offset-2"
  >
    SRS
  </a>
  and
  <a
    href={TECHCART_DOCS.architecture}
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    class="font-medium text-accent underline underline-offset-2"
  >
    architecture
  </a>
  .
</p>
